#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068841 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068448 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/id #uuid "23d66cc8-8e5a-5a33-a7a1-c43f5facdcbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-10833" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$  and $K > 0.$ \n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554818 :question-generator/id #uuid "b524916d-3ce4-55df-b0d1-2926212a3a57" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186068841.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121b603b-942f-556e-b445-2d681ee1ce18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348602} {:answer/id #uuid "500546dd-32e0-5461-ae4c-5e5a7455b919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349173} {:answer/id #uuid "6e22fd1e-737c-5a35-9366-28fb7f8a36bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349458} {:answer/id #uuid "da4666f1-e8ca-5840-a41a-ead889cfbef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+x+C)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350361} {:answer/id #uuid "f06bf25f-3d03-5f76-a7ea-8ddc6224884a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "121b603b-942f-556e-b445-2d681ee1ce18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348602} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1d264b-d2af-5bb5-bbc0-5706b21c43ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "679701a5-b0c3-5865-adfd-e49e046da668" :question/math-academy-id "q-8303" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y}=2x\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "610604c1-be04-5ae1-8759-b50654e72419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349333} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4f4cea-17dd-5832-b0a8-70627738c306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349434} {:answer/id #uuid "6c66c47e-a365-5d7e-8cc6-1deb04431c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349447} {:answer/id #uuid "759561ba-3f4a-5157-8283-98918b52bdbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349529} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2e52a7-5613-5624-ab39-0ecff616a3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2e52a7-5613-5624-ab39-0ecff616a3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350372} :answer-field/id #uuid "26a2711c-7312-535e-b8ec-1d2da18482c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b946e806-cd3a-503b-8b7c-fe17b0906080" :question/math-academy-id "q-8305" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=0$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f680649b-aad0-5c21-b454-2962d171cc58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f680649b-aad0-5c21-b454-2962d171cc58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234935} :answer-field/id #uuid "94bd198b-189e-5b43-a53b-df64554d3cd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "778dd5ee-c1ff-5286-be7b-93fe7ada6aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-128191" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}.$ Assume that $y\\ne 0$ and $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y=-2($ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $+K)^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2C}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}+2C}{2} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+2C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+K} \\\\ y & =-2{({x}^{2}+K)}^{-1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bbb69e0-08ac-541f-a0c9-781e5adaf93d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269951} {:answer/id #uuid "a64073d1-36b3-54ce-9da0-185ff798ba5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270756} {:answer/id #uuid "caeda8f1-2556-5b04-bcc7-d9ae17db2b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271051} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d54641-37a1-5f1b-b411-9374e6a99c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271154} {:answer/id #uuid "f24d04bd-5257-5f28-8f9a-f8dfa0f53d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d54641-37a1-5f1b-b411-9374e6a99c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271154} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58bc506-2ce6-5f14-8138-f2c78e5c6cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8f251269-fa35-5ece-9af4-5538cedc8207" :question/math-academy-id "q-14247" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y+3y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(1+3{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67122d50-92e9-5dbf-990c-0216ba86e1b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270187} {:answer/id #uuid "74a6e407-2886-5e8a-b215-c668e4499333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270298} {:answer/id #uuid "8f18500b-635a-52f2-ad08-9cfecc92fe33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270513} {:answer/id #uuid "afaac117-d7de-54cf-b4d2-12a4f27ad185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270833} {:answer/id #uuid "fe67ce39-75d8-5a64-817a-e44f388af12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe67ce39-75d8-5a64-817a-e44f388af12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271497} :answer-field/id #uuid "df104af1-2216-5c05-8160-ea3f0cd58c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de6a882e-022d-59c5-adf8-2e2394047b45" :question/math-academy-id "q-14253" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(1+2x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =x+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}={x}^{2}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053ca9da-737f-5368-b54e-24f96cafcde5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272436} {:answer/id #uuid "0bac610d-2d04-5604-ae64-cf06296f12ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272493} {:answer/id #uuid "41cc209a-81ce-50b5-9b00-4dc750c10cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272947} {:answer/id #uuid "c69d7489-94d3-50a5-a31f-01511961f376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274110} {:answer/id #uuid "fe66c8fc-fdf6-5a64-96a6-a35189bbdf14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-1/x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe66c8fc-fdf6-5a64-96a6-a35189bbdf14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-1/x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274625} :answer-field/id #uuid "15153a99-fd23-5390-abfe-dedc4885900e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0c7db14-c9c5-588a-b927-09334c1e0842" :question/math-academy-id "q-158009" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\,{y}^{′}-y=3$ for $y\\ne -3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y+3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3|=-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C \\\\ |y+3| & ={e}^{-1/x+C} \\\\ |y+3| & ={e}^{-1/x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y+3| & =K{e}^{-1/x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|y+3| & =K{e}^{-1/x} \\\\ y+3 & =K{e}^{-1/x} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-1/x}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e906697-63fe-5f9c-9695-47b9d1159642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272921} {:answer/id #uuid "491e2dd7-2197-5bca-8669-100af83cb2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273009} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2b0b18-1859-5892-ace0-8191af79d18f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273016} {:answer/id #uuid "92ec8453-5e27-5368-9ac0-a98e23834e02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273663} {:answer/id #uuid "b8730d08-4ef6-5d55-ade2-a86a1a24e46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491e2dd7-2197-5bca-8669-100af83cb2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273009} :answer-field/id #uuid "115fa6bc-8cbf-507c-a94a-1255297d1654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f88ec76-892c-5986-98b6-3866ba9a8457" :question/math-academy-id "q-158010" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y=0$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36403495-4819-509a-932f-4c97f8aa7b1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{2}}+{e}^{{x}^{3}}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324413} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd5ef59-50c9-5c92-95c9-4ed4edd2d608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324625} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa29fba-6a67-5365-afb0-3f19aca8c7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324770} {:answer/id #uuid "c652480f-f0c2-5459-9c4e-e7870338385a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325684} {:answer/id #uuid "d4dff042-5ffc-5451-8cbe-3ca7735819e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd5ef59-50c9-5c92-95c9-4ed4edd2d608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324625} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d052acb-260c-5495-945e-851283aac703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f1ee3e58-1671-5aa8-8cb2-98c85793fdad" :question/math-academy-id "q-3854" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e364992-7edc-53f1-910c-f390251a729e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{K}{x}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345466} {:answer/id #uuid "22166d6d-c75b-5d4d-95dd-c959a62939dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{1}{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345656} {:answer/id #uuid "a530df5f-1758-5257-88f9-0923a1b1b0c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{K+\\frac{1}{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346791} {:answer/id #uuid "c7fec27b-d196-52e9-95f2-c4377198d22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{K-\\frac{2}{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347091} {:answer/id #uuid "d8069f30-9bf0-5b4e-9f9e-9c10ba0b9d32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8069f30-9bf0-5b4e-9f9e-9c10ba0b9d32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347253} :answer-field/id #uuid "316512c9-9dd3-57da-a367-ec001996e486" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7875009d-90d4-5d80-94fc-0c8d789c5fc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-79660" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $(xy)^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(xy)^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}=C-\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3} & =C-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3C-\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{3C-\\frac{3}{x}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=3C.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce8d-6961-5e39-bc06-a013c948432b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345433} {:answer/id #uuid "5564c19a-cbe2-58bc-ba00-963c24b8358a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346075} {:answer/id #uuid "614aee15-ac05-53b6-ba2c-564ddddc0d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346195} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0a5e6f-53c5-57f6-ab14-08940078f3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{6x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346420} {:answer/id #uuid "bbeca412-cbe7-524d-9ed5-77012bdbf6fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "614aee15-ac05-53b6-ba2c-564ddddc0d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346195} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfb7e4f2-96b5-5898-b4a9-72b2a6f8b019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "723d85e2-15cf-520f-80d9-dfe4f98e64df" :question/math-academy-id "q-79663" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2xy=3{x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-2xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}y+2xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+2x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007ed2e6-bd51-5024-8a95-96aa09f05e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345357} {:answer/id #uuid "9e50d021-a50c-5e77-832f-1a3dc9472b6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346729} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f321b9-654c-59f1-9a98-a1f9fbd24b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346835} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4a829c-cabc-5c66-816d-f53731b75309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347005} {:answer/id #uuid "cfbd2b2e-b768-5790-8750-258301711938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{C}{2{x}^{3}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e50d021-a50c-5e77-832f-1a3dc9472b6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346729} :answer-field/id #uuid "031df737-e5b5-5c2a-8346-08d047fd5540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9654e7b6-ccd8-562c-817c-0c6175953f88" :question/math-academy-id "q-79664" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}=6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-{y}^{2} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{y}^{2} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(6{x}^{2}+1){y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =2{x}^{3}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}=2{x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d16c4a6-ec99-5254-95d5-c2498c545a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({x}^{3}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346012} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c2462b-f997-5c04-b171-95ec7c69c289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346834} {:answer/id #uuid "aea245a2-f864-583c-93ae-1ffebcc63b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3/2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346874} {:answer/id #uuid "ba319483-e1c6-5bee-ad75-c8afa87e7451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346969} {:answer/id #uuid "ec814b88-7549-5acd-8292-f5bca233d961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9c2462b-f997-5c04-b171-95ec7c69c289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346834} :answer-field/id #uuid "798d40ee-1bd1-5a20-9b4d-e3b5e219a75d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a2bae15-170e-5e1c-8377-f10d9fc5ad9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79665" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,{y}^{′}=1$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}{y}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{1/2}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{C}{2})}^{2} \\\\ y & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{C}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1427b6f0-45ab-57a3-bbd6-50d52ab7a525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345522} {:answer/id #uuid "15670b68-e9a4-5267-aa5c-b0e904fefa0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345535} {:answer/id #uuid "162c82c1-f74e-5083-bbf9-1dde8b71d2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345546} {:answer/id #uuid "38d35db6-1978-5ad0-9ced-f96355824add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345836} {:answer/id #uuid "89c06b6b-e914-552e-af45-057aa20eba1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89c06b6b-e914-552e-af45-057aa20eba1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346546} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f852ec-a1f8-56f5-8679-e9e9f08dfd90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d00a6660-7238-556d-8857-0bdcf8cbff05" :question/math-academy-id "q-79666" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y}=0$ for $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} \\\\ 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2y\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0084b0-93d4-5ac2-ae43-c8efadc132bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{1/3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349592} {:answer/id #uuid "7f62d026-75e5-5768-912a-ed4fbc3613ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{1/2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349615} {:answer/id #uuid "91edbc26-60f5-5d18-b7c2-4b6f55811b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349751} {:answer/id #uuid "921e26e7-3d47-5dac-b41a-956375d6101d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349755} {:answer/id #uuid "a71d7811-e797-50e1-978f-9b13629b9fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={({x}^{2/3}+K)}^{1/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91edbc26-60f5-5d18-b7c2-4b6f55811b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349751} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7df14ce-0a3a-5b35-9828-40dbb7064dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4faf034-eb8a-55d3-93d9-79b525a402a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-8304" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2}=2{x}^{1/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & =3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2})}^{2/3} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{3C}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053a30cb-744f-52a3-aaa9-5e9e81bf11f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554776} {:answer/id #uuid "06462b90-1d0f-5fe4-a68a-342522cfc531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554777} {:answer/id #uuid "0c2a2c6e-ec32-5cea-805b-d22ac98053a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{K}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554778} {:answer/id #uuid "3bca19c9-c5ff-5a03-b2b3-062714a4d747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554782} {:answer/id #uuid "ac436b3f-83c2-5c6e-ab75-9264f928e89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K - x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06462b90-1d0f-5fe4-a68a-342522cfc531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554777} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24b3c92-af3d-5004-8811-289588535aa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "166df804-4445-53ef-8213-cafc16efa8f7" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+1y=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+1y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475b7c95-614f-5077-bced-4b9b31077014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554785} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6219a6-d622-59d1-8986-4253dd916b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554790} {:answer/id #uuid "945c6768-8894-517a-abc7-51f95ec1b2e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + 6 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554800} {:answer/id #uuid "c80d4c44-6df3-5f21-80b1-61ccf01fb4a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554812} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb372c3-9c93-5ad1-bf5a-a0b171230498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffb372c3-9c93-5ad1-bf5a-a0b171230498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554817} :answer-field/id #uuid "740b783d-ec67-526d-a1bc-1d35f6175189" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83abebcd-929f-55a9-a148-d27778f5afb1" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-6y=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-6y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =6 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=6 x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =6 x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{6 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{6 x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7b053c-d923-595c-8436-02149b0390ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554783} {:answer/id #uuid "95d62561-ff51-58c3-b0d5-acccd5a59f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554801} {:answer/id #uuid "a8de1130-c0a9-59bd-a338-4887563a0037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554803} {:answer/id #uuid "abb416b9-0fa8-57dd-a01e-e19606f19afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554804} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f6b842-e80e-541c-9ec3-28a2725bc8b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f7b053c-d923-595c-8436-02149b0390ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554783} :answer-field/id #uuid "86288c86-69a9-5332-8284-b2e77b50cc38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "927a0bdd-b0c8-54e0-a421-a7cb95e37402" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-2y=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-2y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =2 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=2 x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =2 x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{2 x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{2 x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{2 x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a830d1-b55d-511e-aea9-005f1a3e7827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\sqrt{x^{3} + 4 x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554787} {:answer/id #uuid "8a535be6-5fd0-59ea-93c1-018e7f1b5796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{3 x^{2} + 8 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554796} {:answer/id #uuid "8d969452-2164-5cbe-98bf-bf05149a3635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 8 x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554797} {:answer/id #uuid "929b160c-5f08-5021-837d-b9e46e9dd224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{x^{3} + 4 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554799} {:answer/id #uuid "bf70bdc8-275d-511f-b43b-88bb3a9a1709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x + 8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "929b160c-5f08-5021-837d-b9e46e9dd224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{x^{3} + 4 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554799} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22ac4a5-83ff-5e96-a7cf-68957227ebfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "abbee2f4-ef8f-5ddd-8e7c-80fb454556f0" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-8xy=3{x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-8xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}y+8xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+8x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}+8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11295145-9232-532b-9a91-62d09e45ea7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554779} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5c9f23-b6f4-5911-b0e5-a61aab827692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + 6 x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554788} {:answer/id #uuid "79f6e213-4523-57a9-a155-dd7c4558da22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554793} {:answer/id #uuid "982ff9b1-ae32-5e5a-a7dc-2b576b8754e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{12 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554802} {:answer/id #uuid "c387edae-57a2-5e79-9e57-5be3f5cdab34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + e^{6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11295145-9232-532b-9a91-62d09e45ea7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554779} :answer-field/id #uuid "7064be0c-9bce-501a-839a-b7be939751a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c07fc15d-92cf-5d4a-ac3d-da89047e596d" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-12 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-12 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-12 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =6 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=6 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =6 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{6 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{6 x^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0c8803-ed1b-536f-b7ca-00812a0d163a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 10 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554781} {:answer/id #uuid "426cbd07-ea11-56ec-8fa7-9cc9746a26c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554784} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc067a4-b7f1-5870-815a-7f5f267e4aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K - 5 x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554786} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4e7942-9a87-59d4-aa6f-35749812b466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- 5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554789} {:answer/id #uuid "ef989fea-7778-58d0-bba3-3580cd3ba156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef989fea-7778-58d0-bba3-3580cd3ba156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554815} :answer-field/id #uuid "d485564e-e2b5-5d4a-867b-67459d0784ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccb19ba7-ab90-583c-beff-0f39685096e1" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+10 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+10 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+10 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 10 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 10 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- 10 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- 10 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- 5 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- 5 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- 5 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 5 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 5 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- 5 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- 5 x^{2}}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}]}
